course: dictionary
lesson: 12111
title: Collapsible: folds up small
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «The camping chair is collapsible, so it fits in the boot of the car.» The sentence tells you the chair can be folded up small when you are not using it. So collapsible means able to fold or push down into a smaller shape.
explain: Look inside the word. Collapse means to fold in or fall down, and -ible means able to be. So collapsible means able to fold in. Breaking a word into parts is a clue you can use with other words too.
explain: The word can also mean likely to fold in when hit hard. «The car has a collapsible steering column that folds in a crash to protect the driver.» The clues are crash and protect: the part folds on purpose to keep people safe.
fact: Collapsible means able to be folded or pushed down into a smaller shape when it is not being used.
fact: «Mia's collapsible water bottle folds flat when it is empty.»
fact: Collapsible can also mean likely to fold in or fall down, especially on purpose for safety.
fact: The word comes from collapse, which means to fold in or fall down.
fact: Clue words like folds, flat, smaller and safety show you what collapsible means.
exercise: «The camping chair is collapsible, so it fits in the boot of the car.» What does collapsible mean here? | *Able to fold up small | Painted bright red | Made of glass | Very heavy and hard to move
exercise: «The steering column is collapsible to protect the driver in a crash.» What does collapsible suggest about the column? | *It can fold in on purpose to absorb a crash | It is never able to move | It is very shiny | It makes the car go faster
exercise: Which word is inside collapsible? | collide | *collapse | collar | collect
test: Mia packs her collapsible cup in her bag. What does collapsible help her do? | Make it louder | Fill it with more water | *Fold it flat to save space | Paint it a new colour
test: The designers made a collapsible crate for the market stall. Which is the best meaning of collapsible? | Very tall and thin | Always wet | *Able to be folded flat when not in use | Hard to see through
exam: «The collapsible umbrella folded down small enough for her pocket.» What does the sentence show collapsible means? | Heavy and made of stone | Bright and shiny | *Folds down to a smaller size | Very loud
